@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Busy}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Quirks_Issues}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Quirks_Issues</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Quirks_Issues</h1>

    <p>
        Below are all the quirks and/or issues that I experienced whilst testing the Live Region Services using the Busy Indicator component.
    </p>

</section>

<section class="section-box">
    <h2 id="screen-reader-issues">Screen reader issues</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="screen-reader-issues">
        <li>
            <b>macOS/iPhone</b> paired with <b>Safari.</b> When tested via the Busy Indicator component. The first of two messages got clipped when there was only a 1 second delay between the messages.
            All other screen reader browser pairing that I tested handled this short delay, not that I would advise using such a short delay between messages.
            <p>
                <strong>Note:</strong> I currently have no plans on addressing this as its more of an edge case and the messages can be read in full from using the announcement history dialog.
            </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Busy}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Busy_Short_Delay_Test}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Short_Delay_Test</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_Path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_NavGroup}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview_Tests}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_NavGroup - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview_Tests</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>

